  <article class="container flex-shrink-0" role="main"><div id="main"><div id="culturesmith-front_door-content-view" class="card-slot content-view ALL ALL_PLUS TYPE-rich_text RIGHT-front_door TYPE_PLUS_RIGHT-project-front_door SELF-culturesmith-front_door d0-card-content" data-card-id="53215" data-card-name="Culturesmith+Front Door" data-card-type-id="3" data-card-type-name="RichText" data-card-link-name="Culturesmith+Front_Door" data-slot-id="b4ff5b18ac552f09ebf8" data-slot="{&quot;view&quot;:&quot;content&quot;,&quot;nest_name&quot;:&quot;_main&quot;,&quot;nest_syntax&quot;:&quot;_main|content&quot;,&quot;main&quot;:true,&quot;home_view&quot;:&quot;content&quot;,&quot;main_view&quot;:true,&quot;layout&quot;:&quot;Front Door Layout&quot;}"><h2>All of business and life is a sea of conflict. Most organizations improvise. We give them a jumpstart.</h2>
<p><strong>Conflict done well.</strong></p>
<p>Are you a student, or are you an organization?</p>
<p><div id="culturesmith-front_door-student_door-content-view" class="card-slot content-view ALL ALL_PLUS TYPE-rich_text RIGHT-student_door TYPE_PLUS_RIGHT-rich_text-student_door SELF-culturesmith-front_door-student_door d0-card-content" data-card-id="53217" data-card-name="Culturesmith+Front Door+Student Door" data-card-type-id="3" data-card-type-name="RichText" data-card-link-name="Culturesmith+Front_Door+Student_Door" data-slot-id="bb32c69f1808fe013617" data-slot="{&quot;view&quot;:&quot;content&quot;,&quot;nest_name&quot;:&quot;Culturesmith+Front Door+Student Door&quot;,&quot;nest_syntax&quot;:&quot;Culturesmith+Front Door+Student Door&quot;,&quot;show&quot;:[&quot;content&quot;],&quot;home_view&quot;:&quot;content&quot;}"><p><strong>Here to practise.</strong></p>
<p><strong>I am a student.</strong></p>
<p>The Library holds every recorded class, searchable, with the handbook alongside.</p>
<p><a href="https://culturesmith-library.bunny.run">Go to the Library</a></p></div></p>
<p><div id="culturesmith-front_door-organization_door-content-view" class="card-slot content-view ALL ALL_PLUS TYPE-rich_text RIGHT-organization_door TYPE_PLUS_RIGHT-rich_text-organization_door SELF-culturesmith-front_door-organization_door d0-card-content" data-card-id="53219" data-card-name="Culturesmith+Front Door+Organization Door" data-card-type-id="3" data-card-type-name="RichText" data-card-link-name="Culturesmith+Front_Door+Organization_Door" data-slot-id="4462f74bff4e31d5fbc3" data-slot="{&quot;view&quot;:&quot;content&quot;,&quot;nest_name&quot;:&quot;Culturesmith+Front Door+Organization Door&quot;,&quot;nest_syntax&quot;:&quot;Culturesmith+Front Door+Organization Door&quot;,&quot;show&quot;:[&quot;content&quot;],&quot;home_view&quot;:&quot;content&quot;}"><p><strong>Here for my team.</strong></p>
<p><strong>I am an organization.</strong></p>
<p>Conflict Done Well brings Aikido, Martial Nonviolence, and Peace Practices to schools, hospitals, and teams.</p>
<p><a class="known-card" href="/Conflict_Done_Well"><span class="card-title" title="Conflict Done Well">Conflict Done Well</span></a></p>
<p><a class="known-card" href="/Make_Contact"><span class="card-title" title="Make Contact">Make Contact</span></a></p></div></p>
<p><div id="culturesmith-front_door-way_in-content-view" class="card-slot content-view ALL ALL_PLUS TYPE-rich_text RIGHT-way_in TYPE_PLUS_RIGHT-rich_text-way_in SELF-culturesmith-front_door-way_in d0-card-content" data-card-id="53221" data-card-name="Culturesmith+Front Door+Ways In" data-card-type-id="3" data-card-type-name="RichText" data-card-link-name="Culturesmith+Front_Door+Ways_In" data-slot-id="696edf0df71d5baf1cdd" data-slot="{&quot;view&quot;:&quot;content&quot;,&quot;nest_name&quot;:&quot;Culturesmith+Front Door+Ways In&quot;,&quot;nest_syntax&quot;:&quot;Culturesmith+Front Door+Ways In&quot;,&quot;show&quot;:[&quot;content&quot;],&quot;home_view&quot;:&quot;content&quot;}"><h3>Three ways to be here</h3>
<p>Guest, Member, and Student.</p>
<p><a href="https://culturesmith-library.bunny.run/classes">Going straight to the classes? Browse every recorded class by month</a></p>
<p>Not sure? The Library is an example of all of conflict done well. <a href="https://culturesmith-library.bunny.run">Start there</a>.</p></div></p>
<p><div id="culturesmith-front_door-the_method-content-view" class="card-slot content-view ALL ALL_PLUS TYPE-rich_text RIGHT-the_method TYPE_PLUS_RIGHT-rich_text-the_method SELF-culturesmith-front_door-the_method d0-card-content" data-card-id="53223" data-card-name="Culturesmith+Front Door+The Method" data-card-type-id="3" data-card-type-name="RichText" data-card-link-name="Culturesmith+Front_Door+The_Method" data-slot-id="d38e9f01f96f546557bf" data-slot="{&quot;view&quot;:&quot;content&quot;,&quot;nest_name&quot;:&quot;Culturesmith+Front Door+The Method&quot;,&quot;nest_syntax&quot;:&quot;Culturesmith+Front Door+The Method&quot;,&quot;show&quot;:[&quot;content&quot;],&quot;home_view&quot;:&quot;content&quot;}"><h3>What Conflict Done Well is made of</h3>
<p><a class="known-card" href="/aikido"><span class="card-title" title="Aikido">Aikido</span></a>, <a class="known-card" href="/Martial_Nonviolence"><span class="card-title" title="Martial Nonviolence">Martial Nonviolence</span></a>, and <a class="known-card" href="/Peace_Practices"><span class="card-title" title="Peace Practices">Peace Practices</span></a>.</p>
<h3>Where the method comes from</h3>
<p>Aikido is the source of the method, and the reason the method is credible.</p></div></p>
<p><div id="culturesmith-front_door-community_standard-content-view" class="card-slot content-view ALL ALL_PLUS TYPE-rich_text RIGHT-community_standard TYPE_PLUS_RIGHT-rich_text-community_standard SELF-culturesmith-front_door-community_standard d0-card-content" data-card-id="53225" data-card-name="Culturesmith+Front Door+Community Standard" data-card-type-id="3" data-card-type-name="RichText" data-card-link-name="Culturesmith+Front_Door+Community_Standard" data-slot-id="e66f022533ed9453da78" data-slot="{&quot;view&quot;:&quot;content&quot;,&quot;nest_name&quot;:&quot;Culturesmith+Front Door+Community Standard&quot;,&quot;nest_syntax&quot;:&quot;Culturesmith+Front Door+Community Standard&quot;,&quot;show&quot;:[&quot;content&quot;],&quot;home_view&quot;:&quot;content&quot;}"><h3>A community standard</h3>
<p>Guardians of Peace is an open proposal to the world: a community standard, not a product.</p>
<p><a class="known-card" href="/Guardians_of_Peace"><span class="card-title" title="Guardians of Peace">Guardians of Peace</span></a></p>
<h3>Certification</h3>
<p>Conflict Done Well Certified is for the practitioner. Peace Practices Approved is for the organization that runs the practice.</p>
<p>Both names descend from the Guardians of Peace Credential, proposed in 2010.</p></div></p>
<p><div id="culturesmith-front_door-about_this_build-content-view" class="card-slot content-view ALL ALL_PLUS TYPE-rich_text RIGHT-about_this_build TYPE_PLUS_RIGHT-rich_text-about_this_build SELF-culturesmith-front_door-about_this_build d0-card-content" data-card-id="53227" data-card-name="Culturesmith+Front Door+About This Build" data-card-type-id="3" data-card-type-name="RichText" data-card-link-name="Culturesmith+Front_Door+About_This_Build" data-slot-id="5359c07e1137a37f476c" data-slot="{&quot;view&quot;:&quot;content&quot;,&quot;nest_name&quot;:&quot;Culturesmith+Front Door+About This Build&quot;,&quot;nest_syntax&quot;:&quot;Culturesmith+Front Door+About This Build&quot;,&quot;show&quot;:[&quot;content&quot;],&quot;home_view&quot;:&quot;content&quot;}"><h3>What is real here</h3>
<p>Real: the universal-conflict framing, the question, the three components of Conflict Done Well, the three ways to be here, the Guardians of Peace proposal, and the two certification names. The links point at the working library and at pages in this deck.</p>
<p>Sketch: the front door running inside the demo copy of the engine, on this machine, on a loopback address. The live site is untouched.</p>
<p>Written with an AI agent from Brandon's recorded design rules and the five front-door mockups. The selection, the arrangement and the connecting wording are the agent's; the framing and the question are Brandon's own words, from the working sessions of 2026-10-16 and 2026-10-20.</p></div></p></div></div></article>
